Windows: HIWAVE_CONSOLE_LOG named no file for a Windows path. console_file::setting() takes a value
with a `/` as a path and nothing else (upstream R1 nit 4 lists `C:\logs\console.jsonl` as "not a path"), so
`C:\logs\c.jsonl`, the way every path is written here, did nothing. On Windows a backslash makes it a path
too. Found by refresh #20: console_file_tests::the_variable_alone_names_the_file and
the_process_reads_the_variable_and_set_path_wins (their temp-dir paths have backslashes) failed here, as
they do on a clean hiwave-macos 295ce9f4 on this machine.

Remove when upstream takes the Windows separator (row filed from refresh #20).

--- a/crates/rustkit-engine/src/console_file.rs
+++ b/crates/rustkit-engine/src/console_file.rs
@@ -65,7 +65,9 @@ pub(crate) enum Setting {
 
 pub(crate) fn setting(value: &std::ffi::OsStr) -> Setting {
     let bytes = value.as_encoded_bytes();
-    if bytes.contains(&b'/') {
+    // A separator makes it a path: `/`, and on Windows `\` too, which every path there uses
+    // (`C:\logs\c.jsonl` named no file and the variable did nothing).
+    if bytes.contains(&b'/') || (cfg!(windows) && bytes.contains(&b'\\')) {
         return Setting::File(PathBuf::from(value));
     }
     // `1`, `0`, and the bare words people set a switch to (`true`, `on`).
